  "id": "inherited-date-mismatch-does-not-eliminate",
  "added": "2026-09-21",
  "why": "T3 (compare-spec 2.13.0). The submitted Episode carries its SERIES' release year, inherited when the registry built its full record (provenance ReleaseDate: inherited), and the candidate -- same parent, same distribution number, same title, director and length -- has its own air date four years later. A series' date on an episode says nothing about WHICH episode it is, so the mismatch must not eliminate the candidate (operator rule, CLAUDE.md Future work 2): the field leaves the denominator and the pair scores on what the episode itself asserts. Before 2.13.0 the same pair scored 57.9 Review on a date that was never the episode's. score_min 90 pins the exemption: a scorer that still penalises an inherited mismatch cannot reach it. The `provenance` block is the shared builder's map, added to the fixture format in the same cycle.",
